  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/pack/PackReader.java follows Iris's rules
  for finding a pack's "shaders" folder (net.irisshaders.iris.Iris, loadExternalZipShaderpack),
  for which file extensions are programs
  (net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.include.ShaderPackSourceNames), and for mapping worlds to
  folders from dimension.properties or from the world0 / world-1 / world1 folder names
  (net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.ShaderPack). Changed: the "shaders" folder search is
  depth-limited and sorted, where Iris's has no limit and no fixed order.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/pack/PackInfo.java (folderFor, worldKey)
  follows Iris's choice of the folder that draws a world: a world named in the map keeps its
  id, otherwise the End's or the Overworld's sky makes it the End or the Overworld
  (net.irisshaders.iris.Iris.getCurrentDimension); the named folder if it holds programs,
  else the folder of "*", else the shaders/ root (ShaderPack.getProgramSet and its base
  program set); names without a namespace get "minecraft:" (materialmap.NamespacedId).

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/pack/ProgramSwitches.java follows Iris's
  program.<folder>/<name>.enabled directives: the key's program part
  (net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.properties.ShaderProperties.handleProgramEnabledDirective),
  a switched-off program treated as missing (ShaderPack's source provider), and the value as
  a boolean expression (parsing.BooleanParser: ! && || and brackets, literals true/1 and
  false/0, AND before OR), with unknown names counting as on
  (option.values.OptionValues.getBooleanValueOrDefault). Changed: our own recursive-descent
  parser instead of Iris's two stacks.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/pack/IncludeExpander.java follows Iris's
  #include rules: how an include line is recognized and its path resolved
  (net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.include.FileNode and AbsolutePackPath), and that every
  include is expanded before #if is evaluated, so a cycle is an error
  (net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.include.IncludeGraph). Changed: a cap on total lines
  written and on nesting depth, which Iris doesn't have.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/pack/GlslPreprocessor.java adapts a
  technique from net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.preprocessor.JcppProcessor and
  GlslCollectingListener (which credit GlShader from Canvas, LGPL): #version and #extension
  are hidden from JCPP as #warning lines, so only the ones on live lines come back, and they
  are then hoisted to the top of the output. Changed: our own marker names, our own handling
  of the warning text, and JCPP errors are collected and reported instead of logged.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/pack/StandardDefines.java contains the
  render stage table (names and their order) of the enum
  net.irisshaders.iris.pipeline.WorldRenderingPhase, used as MC_RENDER_STAGE_* values, and
  formats MC_VERSION and IRIS_VERSION the way
  net.irisshaders.iris.gl.shader.StandardMacros.formatVersionString does. Which other names
  are defined is our own choice, documented in the file.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/glsl/ProgramTranslator.java follows two
  Iris rules: the DRAWBUFFERS / RENDERTARGETS comment directive, where the last one in the
  program wins (net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.parsing.CommentDirectiveParser, as described
  in Vitrail's docs/translation.md); and the set of core-profile names Iris supplies when a
  pack uses them without declaring them (projectionMatrix, modelViewMatrix, vaPosition,
  vaNormal, ...; net.irisshaders.iris.pipeline.transform.transformer.CompositeCoreTransformer,
  SodiumCoreTransformer and VanillaCoreTransformer). Changed: those names are only declared
  so the program compiles. Iris's replacement expressions aren't reproduced.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/uniform/GameUniforms.java reproduces how
  Iris computes each value it supplies, quirks included, from net.irisshaders.iris.uniforms
  SystemTimeUniforms (frameTime truncated to whole milliseconds, frameTimeCounter wrapping at
  3600, frameCounter at 720720), ViewportUniforms, WorldTimeUniforms (the Nether and the End
  keep moving time), CelestialUniforms.getSunAngle, CameraUniforms (near = 0.05, far = render
  distance x 16, and the CameraPositionTracker shift by multiples of 30000) and CommonUniforms
  (isEyeInWater, blindness, darknessFactor, nightVision incl. conduit power, is_invisible,
  playerMood, eyeBrightness, screenBrightness, rainStrength, skyColor). Changed: nightVision
  checks for the effect first instead of relying on Iris's mixin into
  GameRenderer.nightVisionScale (same result in vanilla).

  GameUniforms.java also reproduces wetness from net.irisshaders.iris.uniforms.transforms
  .SmoothedFloat and PackDirectives (defaults 600/200, the 0.1 factor, and the bug where
  drynessHalflife sets the rising half-life), and biome / biome_precipitation from
  net.irisshaders.iris.uniforms.BiomeUniforms.

  GameUniforms.java also follows net.irisshaders.iris.uniforms.IrisExclusiveUniforms
  (eyePosition, relativeEyePosition, playerLookVector, cloudHeight, isElytraFlying, heavyFog,
  lightningBoltPosition, endFlashIntensity via EndFlashStorage) and IdMapUniforms (heldItemId,
  heldBlockLightValue for both hands, with the item light rule of
  net.irisshaders.iris.api.v0.item.IrisItemLightProvider). Changed: old hand light isn't applied
  yet. velocity is deliberately not supplied, because Iris 26.3 defines it in
  HardcodedCustomUniforms but never calls that.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/pack/ItemIds.java follows
  net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.IdMap.parseIdMap and materialmap.NamespacedId for
  item.properties: "minecraft:" by default, block-state entries skipped, -1 for unlisted items.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/uniform/RenderMatrices.java reproduces how
  Iris supplies the gbuffer matrices: gbufferModelView is the camera's view rotation and
  gbufferProjection the game's projection passed through the formula of
  net.irisshaders.iris.helpers.MatrixUtils.undoRevZ (net.irisshaders.iris.mixin.MixinLevelRenderer),
  each with an inverse and last frame's value (net.irisshaders.iris.uniforms.MatrixUniforms).
  render/PackChain.java converts depth with Iris's rule from
  net.irisshaders.iris.pipeline.transform.transformer.DepthTransformer (depth reads become
  1 - depth), applied once to the image as Vitrail's docs/translation.md describes.
  glsl/ProgramTranslator.java follows the same class for the fragment stages of passes drawn
  onto the game's reversed-Z depth (terrain, game draws, the sky; not the shadow pass): the
  pack's gl_FragCoord becomes vec4(gl_FragCoord.xy, 1.0 - gl_FragCoord.z, gl_FragCoord.w).
  Changed: done on our token stream; gl_FragDepth writes aren't inverted (not handled yet).

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/uniform/BiomeIds.java and
  mixin/BiomesMixin.java number biomes in vanilla registration order and name them
  BIOME_<PATH>, as net.irisshaders.iris.mixin.MixinBiomes and
  net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.IrisDefines do.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/pack/PropertiesPreprocessor.java adapts the
  technique of net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.preprocessor.PropertiesPreprocessor (which
  credits GlShader from Canvas, LGPL): lines trimmed, non-directive '#' lines and '#' chars
  removed, backslashes hidden from JCPP. Changed: our own marker. The defines it is given
  (pack options that are on, then the game's, then every value option) follow
  PropertiesPreprocessor.preprocessSource's order.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/pack/PackOptions.java follows Iris's shader
  pack options: which lines are options and how a line is read
  (net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.option.OptionAnnotatedSource, parsing.ParsedString,
  StringOption.create, the VALID_CONST_OPTION_NAMES table), on/off options counted only when
  tested by a bare #ifdef/#ifndef in the same weakly connected include group
  (ShaderPackOptions), the starting program names of the include graph
  (include.ShaderPackSourceNames, loading.ProgramId / ProgramArrayId / ProgramGroup), dropping
  a name with two different defaults (OptionSet.Builder, MergedBooleanOption /
  MergedStringOption), reading values (values.MutableOptionValues), and editing the lines
  (OptionAnnotatedSource.edit / editConst / setBooleanDefineValue). The settings file name and
  format follow net.irisshaders.iris.Iris.loadExternalShaderpack / tryReadConfigProperties.
  Changed: our own code and records; the settings file is only read, never rewritten; profiles
  aren't supported; components and files are visited in sorted order where Iris uses hash
  order; a changed line is marked "Luxium: changed option".

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/pack/PackDirectives.java follows the order
  in which net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.programs.ProgramSet.locateDirectives reads const
  directives from fragment stages.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/uniform/Formula.java and CustomUniforms.java
  are our own parser and evaluator for custom uniforms. They follow the behavior of Iris's
  net.irisshaders.iris.uniforms.custom.CustomUniforms, net.irisshaders.iris.parsing.IrisFunctions
  and net.irisshaders.iris.parsing.SmoothFloat: int/float typing, if/in/smooth and the math
  functions, smooth's 0.1 factor and unsmoothed first value, dependency ordering, and dropping
  broken formulas with their dependents. Iris's expression library (kroppeb.stareval) was not
  copied; the operator precedence is the usual C one.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/pack/RenderTargetPlan.java contains Iris's
  table of buffer format names (net.irisshaders.iris.gl.texture.InternalTextureFormat), mapped
  onto the game's GpuFormat by us, and follows Iris's buffer directive rules from
  net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.properties.PackRenderTargetDirectives: names colortexN and
  gcolor..gaux4, keys <name>Format / Clear / ClearColor, defaults RGBA and cleared, and the
  32-buffer limit of net.irisshaders.iris.gl.IrisLimits.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/glsl/ProgramTranslator.java, terrain mode
  (translateForTerrain), follows net.irisshaders.iris.pipeline.transform.transformer.
  SodiumTransformer: decoding Sodium's compact chunk vertex (the 20-bit interleaved position,
  the region offset plus the section's place in its region, the texture coordinate with
  u_TexCoordShrink), gl_MultiTexCoord1/2 as the raw light pair scaled by gl_TextureMatrix[1],
  mc_Entity as (id + 1) << 1 | fluid with -1 for an unmapped block, and mc_midTexCoord in
  1/32768 units, each converted to the type the pack declares. The decode helpers themselves
  are Sodium's (see the Sodium entry). The alpha test per pass (solid OFF, cutout HALF_ALPHA)
  comes from net.irisshaders.iris.pipeline.programs.ShaderKey and gl.blending.AlphaTests.
  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/render/TerrainTakeover.java uses Iris's
  lightmap texture matrix (uniforms.builtin.BuiltinReplacementUniforms) and its render stage
  numbers (pipeline.WorldRenderingPhase).

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/sodium/LuxiumChunkVertex.java follows
  net.irisshaders.iris.vertices.sodium.terrain.XHFPTerrainVertex and XHFPModelVertexType for
  what the extra words hold: the mid-texture coordinate encoding, the block id encoding, and
  separateAo's colour (tint with AO in alpha). Our layout differs: the normal and tangent are
  plain signed bytes instead of Iris's octahedral word, and the light pair keeps Sodium's +8.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/pack/BlockIds.java and
  sodium/BlockStateIds.java follow Iris's block.properties rules (shaderpack.IdMap.parseBlockMap,
  shaderpack.materialmap.BlockEntry.parse, BlockMaterialMapping.addBlockStates, and the key order
  of shaderpack.option.OrderBackedProperties): entry shapes with optional namespace and
  property filters, file order, first match wins. Tag entries aren't supported yet.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/pack/PropertiesPreprocessor.java uses Iris's
  exact test for which '#' lines are directives (PropertiesPreprocessor.preprocessSource).

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/render/TerrainTakeover.java (translucent
  terrain) follows Iris for gbuffers_water: the alpha test (ShaderKey SODIUM_TERRAIN_TRANSLUCENT,
  ONE_TENTH_ALPHA, unless the pack's alphaTest.<program> says otherwise), the vanilla
  translucent blend when the pack sets none (ProgramId.Water has no blend override), the
  OptiFine/Iris blend.<program> and blend.<program>.<buffer> directives, and the render stage
  number (WorldRenderingPhase.TERRAIN_TRANSLUCENT). mixin/sodium/DefaultFluidRendererMixin.java
  gives fluid quads the fluid's block id with Iris's fluid bit (SodiumTransformer.replaceMCEntity).

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/glsl/ProgramTranslator.java, draw mode
  (translateForDraw), follows net.irisshaders.iris.pipeline.transform.transformer.
  VanillaTransformer for the game's own draws: gl_ModelViewMatrix and gl_TextureMatrix[0] from
  the DynamicTransforms block (ModelViewMat, TextureMat), gl_Color = Color * ColorModulator,
  gl_MultiTexCoord1/2 = the UV2 light pair, or full light (240, 240) where the format has none.
  render/EntityTakeover.java keys the served draws by RenderPipeline and uses Iris's alpha tests
  for entities (pipeline.programs.ShaderKey ENTITIES_SOLID off, ENTITIES_CUTOUT ONE_TENTH_ALPHA).

  glsl/ProgramTranslator.java turns entityColor into a value the vertex stage reads from the
  overlay texture, as net.irisshaders.iris.pipeline.transform.transformer.EntityPatcher
  .patchOverlayColor does: texelFetch(overlay, UV1), vec4(rgb, 1 - alpha), and rgb zeroed when
  there's no flash. render/EntityTakeover.java falls back from gbuffers_entities_translucent to
  gbuffers_entities as Iris's ProgramId fallback does, and render/PackChain.java honours
  clouds=off as net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.properties.ShaderProperties reads it.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/render/DrawIds.java follows Iris for the
  values of entityId and blockEntityId (0 outside any entity, -1 for one the pack doesn't list;
  blockEntityId is the block.properties id of the block entity's block state), and
  pack/ItemIds.java reads entity.properties with the same rules as item.properties
  (shaderpack.IdMap.parseEntityIdMap). Block entities are drawn with gbuffers_block
  (pipeline.programs.ShaderKey BLOCK_ENTITY, ProgramId.Block, alpha one tenth).
  The special entity names minecraft:current_player (the camera's own player) and
  minecraft:zombie_villager_converting follow
  mixin.entity_render_context.MixinEntityRenderDispatcher. currentRenderedItemId follows
  mixin.entity_render_context.ItemStackStateLayerMixin, MixinItemRenderer, ItemStackStateMixin,
  MixinItemFeatureRenderer and ModelStorage (mixin/ItemLayerRenderStateMixin.java,
  ItemModelResolverMixin.java, ItemStackRenderStateMixin.java, ItemFeatureRendererMixin.java,
  ItemFeatureRendererSubmitMixin.java): the item shown is noted in appendItemLayers, its id is
  current while a layer is submitted (a block item other than a solid bucket uses its block's
  block.properties id and sets blockEntityId to 1; other items item.properties under the model
  component's name or their own; 0 when unlisted), and an item submit keeps the ids for when its
  draws are built. Changed: Iris writes the ids on each vertex; Luxium keeps one value per draw,
  and model and custom-geometry submits keep their ids the same way, with the game's draw list
  split wherever the ids change (mixin/ModelSubmitIdsMixin.java and friends, our own design).

  Particles (render/EntityTakeover.java, mixin/QuadParticleFeatureRendererMixin.java) follow Iris
  for the program chain (shaderpack.loading.ProgramId: particles -> textured_lit -> textured ->
  basic, particles_translucent -> particles), the PARTICLE vertex format and alpha one tenth
  (pipeline.programs.ShaderKey PARTICLES, PARTICLES_TRANS), and the render stage
  (WorldRenderingPhase.PARTICLES).

  Weather (render/EntityTakeover.java, mixin/WeatherEffectRendererMixin.java) follows Iris for
  the program chain (ProgramId: weather -> textured_lit -> textured -> basic), the alpha test
  (ShaderKey WEATHER one tenth, unless alphaTest.<program> says otherwise) and the render stage
  (WorldRenderingPhase.RAIN_SNOW).

  The hand (mixin/GameRendererHandMixin.java, render/EntityTakeover.java, glsl/ProgramTranslator
  Format.handDepth) follows net.irisshaders.iris.pathways.HandRenderer: the hand's depth squeezed
  by DEPTH = 0.125 around the middle (0.4375 + 0.125 d), its own projection (the hud field of
  view), and the program chain (ProgramId: hand -> textured_lit; hand_water -> hand) with alpha
  one tenth (ShaderKey HAND_CUTOUT, HAND_TRANSLUCENT). Running the composites after the hand,
  with its depth in depthtex0, follows Vitrail's docs/frame.md ("The hand is the one family the
  engine has to move rather than intercept").

  The enchantment glint (glsl/ProgramTranslator.java Format.glint, render/EntityTakeover.java
  Glint, pack/StandardDefines.java) follows Iris: gl_TextureMatrix[0] is mat4(1.0) in glint draws
  (pipeline.transform.transformer.VanillaTransformer, isGlint() && hasOverlay()), and the inline
  glint API of pipeline.transform.transformer.GlintTransformer: mc_hasGlint() / mc_sampleGlint()
  (glintAlpha * the glint texture at TextureMat * UV0, or UV3 in the special-glint format, passed
  to the fragment stage as a varying), constants where the draw has no glint; IRIS_INLINE_GLINT is
  defined as gl.shader.StandardMacros does, and glintAlpha is the glint strength option as in
  uniforms.IrisExclusiveUniforms. Which glinted pipelines are served by the base programs follows
  pipeline.IrisPipelines / programs.ShaderKey (the *_GLINT keys use the entity and hand programs).
  Changed: glint draws are told apart by the 26.3 pipeline's GLINT shader define, the texture is
  the game's own GlintSampler, and the strength is a value in Luxium's uniform block.

  Spider eyes, beacon beams and lightning (render/EntityTakeover.java) follow Iris for which
  program serves which pipeline and its fallbacks (shaderpack.loading.ProgramId SpiderEyes,
  BeaconBeam, Lightning; pipeline.programs.ShaderKey EMISSIVE_ENTITIES, BEACON, LIGHTNING), their
  alpha tests (beacon and lightning off) and SpiderEyes' default blend (SRC_ALPHA ONE ZERO ONE).

  Banner and shield patterns and text in the hand (render/EntityTakeover.java) follow
  net.irisshaders.iris.pipeline.IrisPipelines: BANNER_PATTERN goes through getTranslucent
  (ShaderKey BE_TRANSLUCENT, ProgramId.BlockTrans: block_translucent -> block, for a block entity;
  ENTITIES_TRANSLUCENT otherwise; alpha one tenth), and the text pipelines in the hand (a held
  map) through getText (ShaderKey HAND_TEXT: ProgramId.Hand, AlphaTests.NON_ZERO_ALPHA).
  Changed: Luxium draws patterns in the level's solid-feature window, where 26.3 puts them.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/uniform/ShadowMatrices.java follows
  net.irisshaders.iris.shadows.ShadowMatrices (createBaselineModelViewMatrix, snapModelViewToGrid,
  createOrthoMatrix) and ShadowRenderer: the light view's rotations by the sky angle and
  sunPathRotation, the grid snap with Java's signed remainder, the orthographic box of half size
  shadowDistance; shadowAngle as uniforms.CelestialUniforms.getShadowAngle; the defaults and const
  directives of shaderpack.properties.PackShadowDirectives (shadowMapResolution 1024,
  shadowDistance 160, near/far -100.05/156, shadowIntervalSize 2). The shadow pass's alpha tests
  follow ShaderKey SHADOW_SODIUM_TERRAIN_SOLID/CUTOUT and its clear colours the shadowcolor
  defaults (white).

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/render/SkyTakeover.java follows Iris for
  which program draws each vanilla sky pipeline (net.irisshaders.iris.pipeline.IrisPipelines:
  SKY, STARS and SUNRISE_SUNSET with gbuffers_skybasic; CELESTIAL and END_SKY with
  gbuffers_skytextured) and for each piece's render stage (mixin.MixinSkyRenderer and
  mixin.MixinLevelRenderer: SKY, SUNSET, SUN, MOON, STARS, VOID; CUSTOM_SKY for the End's sky
  and End flash, where none of those calls run).

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/render/ShadowCulling.java,
  sodium/ShadowRegion.java and mixin/sodium/RenderRegionMixin.java,
  RenderRegionManagerMixin.java, RenderSectionManagerAccessor.java and
  SodiumWorldRendererAccessor.java follow Iris's shadow render lists on Sodium
  (net.irisshaders.iris.compat.sodium.mixin.MixinRenderRegion, MixinRenderRegionManager,
  MixinRenderSectionManagerShadow, MixinSodiumWorldRenderer, and shadows.ShadowRenderer): a
  second render list and batch map per region swapped in for the shadow pass, every batch
  emptied in all maps wherever Sodium empties one, the light's list filled by Sodium's
  renderOutOfGraph walk, and the camera's lists, tree and task lists put back afterwards.
  Changed: our own code; the walk runs inside our shadow pass rather than through
  SodiumWorldRenderer.setupTerrain, and its frustum is the shadow map's own box (the light's
  clip space) instead of Iris's advanced shadow frustum.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/mixin/LevelExtractorMixin.java (with
  MetalShadersClient.keepImprovedTransparencyOff) follows
  net.irisshaders.iris.mixin.fabulous.MixinDisableFabulousGraphics: while a pack is in use,
  Improved Transparency is switched off and the graphics preset set to Custom, checked at the
  start of LevelExtractor.allChanged and onResourceManagerReload. Changed: also checked once
  when the pack loads.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/render/CustomTextures.java follows Iris's
  texture.<stage>.<sampler> directives: the stage names and what each covers
  (net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.texture.TextureStage: gbuffers includes the shadow
  passes, composite includes final), the sampler name cut at its first dot
  (shaderpack.properties.ShaderProperties), an override matching any of a sampler's names
  (gl.program.ProgramSamplers.CustomTextureSamplerInterceptor), overrides of a render target
  switched off once an earlier pass of the same stage has written it this frame
  (pipeline.CompositeRenderer, flippedAtLeastOnce), PNG filtering from the .mcmeta file,
  nearest and repeat unless "blur" or "clamp" (targets.backed.NativeImageBackedCustomTexture),
  and noisetex read linear and repeating (targets.backed.NativeImageBackedNoiseTexture).
  Changed: raw-texture directives, minecraft: resource paths and customTexture.* aren't
  supported yet and are skipped with a warning.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/mixin/GameRendererRenderMixin.java (the view
  bobbing part) follows net.irisshaders.iris.mixin.MixinModelViewBobbing: while a pack is in
  use, GameRenderer.renderLevel's bobbing matrix and its nausea/portal rotate and scale are kept
  out of the projection and applied to the camera's view rotation (bob x view) before the level
  is drawn. Changed: Luxium also captures gbufferModelView with the bob at setProjectionMatrix.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/mixin/EntityRenderDispatcherMixin.java
  (luxium$keepVanillaShadow) follows net.irisshaders.iris.mixin.MixinEntityRenderDispatcher
  and IrisRenderingPipeline.shouldDisableVanillaEntityShadows: the vanilla blob shadow under
  entities is not submitted while the pack has a shadow pass.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/gui/ShaderPackScreen.java follows the
  behaviour of net.irisshaders.iris.gui.screen.ShaderPackScreen and
  gui.element.ShaderPackSelectionList: a first row that turns shaders on and off and is inactive
  with no packs; clicking a pack selects it and also turns shaders on; the applied pack drawn in
  yellow (0xFFFFF263) and every pack grey (0xFFA2A2A2) while shaders are off; Cancel, Apply and
  Done, with Done and Esc applying; "Open Shader Pack Folder...". The English labels follow
  Iris's en_us.json (assets/luxium/lang/en_us.json). Changed: vanilla's list and buttons instead
  of Iris's own widgets and textures, no transitions, a single footer layout, and no Download,
  drag-and-drop or settings button yet.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/gui/LuxiumKeys.java takes Iris 26.3's default
  key for the screen, I (net.irisshaders.iris.Iris, shaderpackScreenKeybind).

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/mixin/VideoSettingsScreenMixin.java puts a
  "Shader Packs..." button in Video Settings, where Iris puts its own
  (net.irisshaders.iris.mixin.gui.MixinVideoSettingsScreen). Changed: added with
  OptionsList.addBig(AbstractWidget) after the graphics preset, not as a fake OptionInstance.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/gui/LuxiumDebugEntry.java and
  mixin/DebugScreenEntriesMixin.java, mixin/DebugScreenEntryListMixin.java follow how Iris adds
  its F3 lines (net.irisshaders.iris.gui.debug.IrisDebugEntry, mixin.MixinDebugEntries,
  mixin.MixinDebugScreenEntriesList): an entry registered with DebugScreenEntries, shown in the
  overlay unless the player set its status. Changed: one line of our own, with colours.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/sodium/SodiumPrograms.java solves the problem
  net.irisshaders.iris.compat.sodium.mixin.MixinShaderChunkRenderer solves (Sodium's terrain
  pipelines are built once, with the first chunk vertex format). Changed: one set kept per
  format and swapped with it, where Iris always builds them with Sodium's own format.

